Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:19:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/26] ling: the CUDA TP=1 family from #874
 (jschmied/TensorFold ling-family e99e6505), files as he wrote them

The engine, lanes backend, native server hooks, MTP drafter, bf16/FP8/NVFP4 loaders, glue kernels and their
CUDA checks, taken verbatim from the closed PR #874's head. His shared-kernel additions that apply to v1.2.0
as they stand come with them: the FP8 experts' instances in Ling's clamp order (EPI 4) and the FP8 experts'
device packer. This commit alone does not build on v1.2.0; the next one ports it onto main's current GLM
kernels, lanes ABI and host package.
